Let multiple minimap tracking types be active at once (Find Minerals + Find
Herbs simultaneously, etc.), instead of applying one cancelling the other.
Touches: src/server/game/Spells/SpellInfo.cpp, SpellInfo::IsAuraExclusiveBySpecificWith()

Why: WotLK's native minimap tracking can only show one type at a time
purely because of this one switch case -- SPELL_SPECIFIC_TRACKER is listed
as "exclusive with itself," so Aura::CanStackWith (SpellAuras.cpp) refuses
to let a second tracking aura coexist with an existing one, regardless of
which specific resource/creature type each tracks. The client-facing data
model this maps to (PLAYER_TRACK_RESOURCES / PLAYER_TRACK_CREATURES,
AuraEffect::HandleAuraTrackResources/HandleAuraTrackCreatures in
SpellAuraEffects.cpp) already stores tracking state as individual bits
(SetFlag(field, 1 << (MiscValue-1))) -- i.e. it already natively supports
multiple simultaneous tracking types; only this exclusivity check was
stopping more than one from ever being applied. Player wanted Track Ore
and Track Herbs (Living Gear perks) to both show at once, alongside
whatever native tracking (Track Humanoids, etc.) they also have active --
this restores that instead of building a custom minimap-icon system.

--- a/src/server/game/Spells/SpellInfo.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Spells/SpellInfo.cpp
@@ SpellInfo::IsAuraExclusiveBySpecificWith(SpellInfo const* spellInfo)
     switch (spellSpec1)
     {
-        case SPELL_SPECIFIC_TRACKER:
         case SPELL_SPECIFIC_WARLOCK_ARMOR:
         case SPELL_SPECIFIC_MAGE_ARMOR:
